  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5" extension="2015-08-01"/><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5.1" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Sudden collapse with loss of consciousness four days before the visit, after hours of voice recording in a hot booth with the air conditioning off: felt hot and faint, lost consciousness, generalized stiffening then jerking of all four limbs for about a minute, vomiting, and 20 to 30 minutes of confusion; seizure versus convulsive syncope; emergency evaluation the same day</td><td>resolved</td><td>provisional</td>
    <td>R55</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to the documented collapse at the dubbing studio; resolved into a first seizure at the epilepsy clinic when the history, examination, ECG, MRI and EEG were reviewed together. Not a claim about his real symptoms beyond the cited accounts.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>First unprovoked seizure: unknown-onset motor (tonic-clonic) seizure by the ILAE 2017 classification; MRI with epilepsy protocol and sleep-deprived EEG normal, so it does not meet the definition of epilepsy; likely triggers were sleep deprivation, heat, missed meals and cannabis the same day; no antiseizure medicine by shared decision; synthetic modern episode linked to his documented collapse with convulsions</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R56.9</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the epilepsy clinic; the 1973 events and their disputed causes remain D and R.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Chronic low back pain since a weightlifting injury three years ago, reported as an injury to a sacral nerve; worse with long sitting and heavy lifting; no weakness, numbness or bladder or bowel change</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M54.50</td><td>S — Synthetic modern problem anchored to his documented back injury and chronic pain.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

