<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">First unprovoked seizure (R56.9)</content>. No recurrence in five weeks with triggers controlled. Creatine kinase 168 U/L and creatinine 0.96 mg/dL: the muscle breakdown and mild kidney injury after the seizure have resolved. [S]<list><item>Continue without an antiseizure medicine.</item><item>No driving; sleep, meals, heat and fluid plan; no cannabis.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic low back pain (M54.50)</content>. Improving with exercise therapy; pain 3 out of 10. [S]<list><item>Continue the core and motor control program; acetaminophen when needed.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Seizure recurrence, auras, staring spells and jerks on waking (event diary)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No events in five weeks; diary kept</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Neurological examination</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Normal</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Creatine kinase and creatinine after a convulsive seizure with exertion</td><td>Until normal (about one week, then as needed)</td><td>Deferred</td><td>The repeat due about a week after the epilepsy clinic was missed: he was away for work and no laboratory visit was booked for it. Today, five weeks after the seizure, creatine kinase is 168 U/L and creatinine 0.96 mg/dL (eGFR 108), both normal, so no harm resulted. Corrective action: repeat tests are now booked as laboratory visits with a reminder the day before, rather than left to the next clinic visit</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Sodium, glucose, calcium and magnesium</td><td>At the event; repeat if abnormal or with a new event</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sodium 140 mmol/L and glucose 90 mg/dL with the kidney check; potassium 4.3</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>MRI of the brain with an epilepsy protocol</td><td>After a first seizure; repeat only with a new event or finding</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Normal at the epilepsy clinic; no new event</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>EEG (routine, and sleep-deprived if the first is normal or delayed)</td><td>Soon after a first seizure; repeat only with a new event</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Normal at the epilepsy clinic; no new event</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antiseizure medicine decision</td><td>After the evaluation, and again with any new seizure</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No medicine, as decided at the epilepsy clinic</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medicines that lower the seizure threshold or cause withdrawal seizures</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Acetaminophen only; no new medicines</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Triggers: sleep, meals, heat, fluids and electrolytes, alcohol and cannabis</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sleeps about seven hours; regular meals; studio air conditioning and breaks; drinks to thirst with electrolytes; no cannabis</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Driving and dangerous activities</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Not driving; no heights</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Seizure first aid and safety at work</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Studio crew have the first aid handout</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Back pain score (0 to 10) and function</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Back pain 3 out of 10; full training except heavy lifting</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Back examination and red flags (saddle sensation, bladder and bowel, leg strength)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No red flags</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise therapy for chronic low back pain</td><td>Ongoing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Core and motor control program with a physical therapist for three weeks</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>No further seizures. In progress; target 2026-07-13 [S]</item><item>Sleep at least seven hours a night, including on film schedules. Outcome by 2026-06-15: About seven hours a night from the first month [S]</item><item>No cannabis while the seizure risk is highest. In progress; target 2026-07-13 [S]</item><item>Back pain at 3 or less out of 10 with full training. In progress; target 2026-07-13 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Evidence-based guideline: Management of an unprovoked first seizure in adults: Report of the Guideline Development Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology and the American Epilepsy Society (2015); Practice Parameter: evaluating an apparent unprovoked first seizure in adults (an evidence-based review) (2007); Noninvasive Treatments for Acute, Subacute, and Chronic Low Back Pain: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians (2017); Supplementary Health Information Sheet for Driver Assessment (First Schedule of the Road Traffic (Driving Licences) Regulations, Cap. 374B) (2021); Neurological disorders: assessing fitness to drive (first unprovoked epileptic seizure) (2026); First Aid for Seizures (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Two-month review in four weeks. Call at once for any event. Next scheduled visit 2026-06-29: periodic adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
